    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Pythagoras in triangle DCE",
        "body": "$DE=DA=\\sqrt2$ (radii) and $DC=AB=1$. In the right-angled triangle $DCE$, $CE^2=DE^2-DC^2=2-1=1$, so $CE=1$.\n\n**Answer: (E) 1**"
      }
    ],
