        "text": "4"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "5"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "6"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Angle sum",
        "body": "The interior angles of a hexagon sum to $720^\\circ$. Suppose $m$ angles are acute (less than $90^\\circ$); the other $6-m$ angles are each less than $180^\\circ$ (convex). Then $720<90m+180(6-m)=1080-90m$, so $m<4$ and $m\\le3$. Three acute angles are possible: e.g. take a hexagon cut from a long thin triangle-like shape with three angles of $80^\\circ$ and three of $160^\\circ$ ($3\\cdot80+3\\cdot160=720$).\n\n**Answer: (B) 3**"
      }
    ],
