    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "An unknown polynomial yields a remainder of 2 upon division by $x-1$, and a remainder of 1 upon division by $x-2$. If this polynomial is divided by $(x-1)(x-2)$, then the remainder is",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "2"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$x$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$x+1$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "3"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$-x+3$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Remainder theorem",
        "body": "The remainder on division by $(x-1)(x-2)$ has the form $ax+b$, so $P(x)=(x-1)(x-2)q(x)+ax+b$. Then $P(1)=a+b=2$ and $P(2)=2a+b=1$, giving $a=-1$, $b=3$. The remainder is $-x+3$.\n\n**Answer: (E)**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "polynomials"
    ],
    "difficulty": 2,
    "duplicateOf": null,
    "reviewNote": null,
    "wrongPoints": -1
  },
  {
    "id": "samf-senior-2000-r2-14",
    "bank": "samf",
    "source": {
      "contest": "South African Mathematics Olympiad",
