        "text": "1998"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "1999"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "2001"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Count digits",
        "body": "Pages 1-9 use 1 digit each (9 digits), pages 10-99 use 2 each, pages 100-999 use 3 each. A book of $k$ pages with $10\\le k\\le 99$ needs $9+2(k-9)=2k-9$ digits, an odd number up to $189$. A book with $100\\le k\\le999$ pages needs $189+3(k-99)$ digits: $189$ plus a multiple of 3, i.e. a multiple of 3 between $192$ and $2886$.\n\n31 is odd and less than 189 (so $k=20$). 543, 1998 and 2001 are multiples of 3. But 1999 is not a multiple of 3 and exceeds 189, so it is impossible.\n\n**Answer: (D) 1999**"
      }
