    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Midpoint theorem",
        "body": "Since $B$ is fixed and $BC$ has fixed length, $C$ moves on a circle about $B$. The diagonals bisect each other, so the intersection $M$ is the midpoint of $AC$. If $O$ is the midpoint of $AB$ (fixed), then $OM\\parallel BC$ and $OM=\\frac12BC$. So $M$ stays at a fixed distance $\\frac12BC$ from the fixed point $O$: it moves on a circle (or part of one).\n\n**Answer: (A) circle**"
      }
