      {
        "title": "Factor",
        "body": "$\\frac1m+\\frac1n=\\frac1{15}$ gives $15(m+n)=mn$, i.e. $(m-15)(n-15)=225$. Since $m,n>15$ (each of $\\frac1m,\\frac1n<\\frac1{15}$), both factors are positive. $225=3^2\\cdot5^2$ has $3\\cdot3=9$ divisors, each giving exactly one ordered pair.\n\n**Answer: (E) 9**"
